594 - Heir of the Kingdom
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 594
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]Heir of the kingdom, O [F]why dost thou [Bb]slumber?
Why art thou sleeping so [F]near [C7]thy blest [F]home?
Wake thee, a[Bb]rouse thee, and [Eb]gird on thine [Bb]armor,
[Gm]Speed, [F]for the [Bb]moments are [F7]hurrying [Bb]on.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Heir of the [F]kingdom, say, why [Bb]dost thou linger?
[F]How canst thou [C7]tarry in sight [F]of the prize?
[Bb]Up, and [Eb]adorn thee, the [Bb]Savior is coming;
[Gm]Haste [F]to [Bb]receive Him [F7]descending [Bb]the skies.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Earth's mighty [F]nations, in [Bb]strife and commotion,
[F]Tremble with [C7]terror, and [F]sink in dismay;
[Bb]Listen, 'tis [Eb]nought but the [Bb]chariot's loud rumbling;
[Gm]Heir [F]of [Bb]the kingdom, [F7]no [Bb]longer delay.

Verse 4:
[Bb]Stay not, O [F]stay not for [Bb]earth's vain allurements!
[F]See how [C7]its glory [F]is passing away;
[Bb]Break the strong [Eb]fetters the foe [Bb]hath bound o'er thee;
[Gm]Heir [F]of the [Bb]kingdom, [F7]turn, turn [Bb]thee away.

Verse 5:
[Bb]Keep the [F]eye single, the [Bb]head upward lifted;
[F]Watch for [C7]the glory of [F]earth's coming King;
[Bb]Lo! o'er [Eb]the mountaintops light [Bb]is now breaking;
[Gm]Heirs [F]of the [Bb]kingdom, [F7]rejoice ye [Bb]and sing.
